# Source review: one physical port per simultaneous Pauli axis

This review supports the final argument as a conditional finite-Hamiltonian theorem for the simultaneous X/Y/Z sampled program on the one fixed accessible pair c=v0=(0,1,1), e=(0,2,1), restricted to N_X=1. I found no blocking mathematical defect in that bounded claim. The response, both odd counterterms, whole-qubit positivity, global inverse, mixed-excitation correction, bare-input comparison and literal geometry survive the checks below.

The isolation premise is consequential. Fresh and disjoint sites do not eliminate unintended nearest-neighbor edges. The nominal interaction graph must actually be supplied, or every residual interaction must be bounded in the full Hilbert-space norm after physical scaling. The final source includes same-component chords as well as fresh–old and intercomponent edges. The selected count of 35 omitted edges is not a uniform-family count. Neither that enumeration nor the author's 159 selected predicates establishes this review's conclusion.

This is a source-exposed mathematical assessment, not an audit verdict, retained status, physical realization, or acceptance of the full autonomous program. The saturated v1 site, all scheduled pairs, waveform synthesis, initialization/control manufacture, common strength caps and efficient scaling remain outside the established scope.

